{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980273838,"sessionID":"ses_1cc835d50ffen2Kt2wObzNNoV5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_EPZQU2wYkbfxDMCnPSIuPwUw","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"This request comes from the ClinGen Hereditary Cardiovascular Disease Gene Curation Expert Panel (GCEP): https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/ \\n\\nWe are lumping several cardiac phenotypes associated with SCN5A into one new term. Below we provide the information for the updates and reorganization of the terms. \\n\\n1. New Mondo term: SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder\\n\\nParent terms for the new term to reside under:\\ncardiogenetic disease (MONDO:0100547)\\ncardiac rhythm disease MONDO:0007263\\nNew proposed Parent term: cardiogenetic rhythm disorders (Details provided below)\\n\\nPhenotypes (Child terms) INCLUDED under the new term include: \\nAtrial fibrillation, familial, 10 MIM: 614022 (MONDO:0013530)\\nSick sinus syndrome 1 MIM: 608567 (MONDO:0024562)\\nVentricular fibrillation, familial, 1 MIM: 603829 (MONDO:0011376)\\nLong QT syndrome 3 MIM: 603830 (MONDO:0011377)\\nBrugada syndrome 1 MIM: 601144 (MONDO:0011001)\\n\\nPhenotypes EXCLUDED but still associated with SCN5A: \\n{Sudden infant death syndrome, susceptibility to} MIM: 272120\\nHeart block, nonprogressive MIM: 113900\\nHeart block, progressive, type IA MIM: 113900\\nCardiomyopathy, dilated, 1E MIM: 601154\\n\\n\\nNew term description for SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder:\\n\\nA heterogeneous collection of cardiac rhythm disorders caused by genetic variation in the SCN5A gene with autosomal dominant inheritance. Affected individuals are commonly reported to have unremarkable cardiac morphology and at least one cardiac rhythm phenotype that includes, but is not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, long QT syndrome, Brugada syndrome, and multifocal ectopic Purkinje-related premature contractions. Individuals with pathogenic variants in SCN5A may also exhibit overlapping or mixed cardiac rhythm phenotypes and intrafamilial variability.\\n\\n\\n\\n2. New proposed Parent term: cardiogenetic rhythm disorders\\n\\nCardiogene... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87PBfr_\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"LengUNC\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"NONE\",\n10:       \"body\": \"I apologize for the inconvenience. Please remove \\\"multifocal ectopic Purkinje-related premature contractions\\\" from the terms definitions as we are still evaluating the gene-disease association. Please use the revised definitions as below.\\n\\nNew term description for SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder:\\nA heterogeneous collection of cardiac rhythm disorders caused by genetic variation in the SCN5A gene with autosomal dominant inheritance. Affected individuals are commonly reported to have unremarkable cardiac morphology and at least one cardiac rhythm phenotype that includes, but is not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, long QT syndrome, and Brugada syndrome. Individuals with pathogenic variants in SCN5A may also exhibit overlapping or mixed cardiac rhythm phenotypes and intrafamilial variability.\\n\\nNew term description for Cardiogenetic rhythm disorders: \\nA heterogeneous group of cardiac rhythm phenotypes with a monogenic etiology that include, but are not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, Brugada syndrome, long QT syndrome, short QT syndrome, tachycardia with fibrillation, etc.\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-10-31T14:12:09Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [\n16:         {\n17:           \"content\": \"THUMBS_UP\",\n18:           \"users\": {\n19:             \"totalCount\": 1\n20:           }\n21:         }\n22:       ],\n23:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9707#issuecomment-3473275647\",\n24:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n25:     },\n26:     {\n27:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87RwEOk\",\n28:       \"author\": {\n29:         \"login\": \"katiermullen\"\n30:       },\n31:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n32:       \"body\": \"@LengUNC - thank you for this request! I have added the two new terms with the definitions that you provided. \\n\\nFor the children of 'cardiogenetic rhythm disorder' I was able to include all of the terms that you requested EXCEPT atrioventricular block (MONDO:0000465) because this condition does not necessarily have a monogenic etiology. \\n\\nPlease let me know if you require an additional new term that is specifically 'monogenic atrioventricular block'. If so, please kindly provide a source such as PMID or clin gen working group.\\n\\nThank you! \",\n33:       \"createdAt\": \"2025-11-11T22:54:59Z\",\n34:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n35:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n36:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n37:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n38:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9707#issuecomment-3519038372\",\n39:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n40:     }\n41:   ],\n42:   \"title\": \"Mondo request for SCN5A disease entity for ClinGen\",\n43:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9707\"\n44: }\n\n(End of file - total 44 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"This request comes from the ClinGen Hereditary Cardiovascular Disease Gene Curation Expert Panel (GCEP): https://www.clinicalgenome.org/affiliation/40104/ \\n\\nWe are lumping several cardiac phenotypes associated with SCN5A into one new term. Below we provide the information for the updates and reorganization of the terms. \\n\\n1. New Mondo term: SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder\\n\\nParent terms for the new term to reside under:\\ncardiogenetic disease (MONDO:0100547)\\ncardiac rhythm disease MONDO:0007263\\nNew proposed Parent term: cardiogenetic rhythm disorders (Details provided below)\\n\\nPhenotypes (Child terms) INCLUDED under the new term include: \\nAtrial fibrillation, familial, 10 MIM: 614022 (MONDO:0013530)\\nSick sinus syndrome 1 MIM: 608567 (MONDO:0024562)\\nVentricular fibrillation, familial, 1 MIM: 603829 (MONDO:0011376)\\nLong QT syndrome 3 MIM: 603830 (MONDO:0011377)\\nBrugada syndrome 1 MIM: 601144 (MONDO:0011001)\\n\\nPhenotypes EXCLUDED but still associated with SCN5A: \\n{Sudden infant death syndrome, susceptibility to} MIM: 272120\\nHeart block, nonprogressive MIM: 113900\\nHeart block, progressive, type IA MIM: 113900\\nCardiomyopathy, dilated, 1E MIM: 601154\\n\\n\\nNew term description for SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder:\\n\\nA heterogeneous collection of cardiac rhythm disorders caused by genetic variation in the SCN5A gene with autosomal dominant inheritance. Affected individuals are commonly reported to have unremarkable cardiac morphology and at least one cardiac rhythm phenotype that includes, but is not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, long QT syndrome, Brugada syndrome, and multifocal ectopic Purkinje-related premature contractions. Individuals with pathogenic variants in SCN5A may also exhibit overlapping or mixed cardiac rhythm phenotypes and intrafamilial variability.\\n\\n\\n\\n2. New proposed Parent term: cardiogenetic rhythm disorders\\n\\nCardiogene... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87PBfr_\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"LengUNC\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"NONE\",\n      \"body\": \"I apologize for the inconvenience. Please remove \\\"multifocal ectopic Purkinje-related premature contractions\\\" from the terms definitions as we are still evaluating the gene-disease association. Please use the revised definitions as below.\\n\\nNew term description for SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder:\\nA heterogeneous collection of cardiac rhythm disorders caused by genetic variation in the SCN5A gene with autosomal dominant inheritance. Affected individuals are commonly reported to have unremarkable cardiac morphology and at least one cardiac rhythm phenotype that includes, but is not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, long QT syndrome, and Brugada syndrome. Individuals with pathogenic variants in SCN5A may also exhibit overlapping or mixed cardiac rhythm phenotypes and intrafamilial variability.\\n\\nNew term description for Cardiogenetic rhythm disorders: \\nA heterogeneous group of cardiac rhythm phenotypes with a monogenic etiology that include, but are not limited to, atrial fibrillation, sick sinus syndrome, progressive cardiac conduction disease, ventricular fibrillation, Brugada syndrome, long QT syndrome, short QT syndrome, tachycardia with fibrillation, etc.\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-10-31T14:12:09Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [\n        {\n          \"content\": \"THUMBS_UP\",\n          \"users\": {\n            \"totalCount\": 1\n          }","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778980273768,"end":1778980273834}},"id":"prt_e337cbe60001KSm9FeA7j7Jzb2","sessionID":"ses_1cc835d50ffen2Kt2wObzNNoV5","messageID":"msg_e337ca3d5001CLsW974brV5p4E"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980273865,"sessionID":"ses_1cc835d50ffen2Kt2wObzNNoV5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_e7TrQwZbdeYaxaNQmJTmSFI6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"task-coordinator"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"task-coordinator\">\n# Skill: task-coordinator\n\nYou are the MONDO Ontology Task Coordinator, a master planner responsible for orchestrating all ontology work in the MONDO project. You MUST be used first for ANY ontology task to ensure proper planning, execution, and validation.\n\nYour core responsibilities:\n\n1. **Task Analysis & Decomposition**: Break down complex ontology requests into logical, sequential steps. Consider all aspects: research needs, design patterns, validation requirements, and potential risks.\n\n2. **Agent Orchestration**: Plan the optimal sequence of specialized agents:\n   - Start with deep-research-specialist for literature review when PMIDs are mentioned\n   - Use design-pattern-advisor to ensure compliance with MONDO patterns\n   - Coordinate execution agents for the actual ontology work\n   - Always include identifier-validator to prevent hallucinated IDs\n   - End with obo-checkin for term integration\n   - Use ontology-reasoner when logical definitions are involved\n\n3. **Critical Validation Oversight**: You are the final safeguard against:\n   - Hallucinated MONDO IDs, PMIDs, or gene identifiers\n   - Missing required metadata (definitions, sources, proper citations)\n   - Violations of MONDO naming conventions\n   - Incomplete check-in processes\n\n4. **Quality Assurance Protocol**: Ensure every task includes:\n   - Proper literature research when references are provided\n   - Design pattern compliance checking\n   - Identifier validation (especially for genes using HGNC or NCBI gene)\n   - Complete source attribution\n   - Syntax validation before check-in\n   - Reasoner validation for logical definitions\n\n5. **Risk Management**: Flag high-risk scenarios:\n   - New term creation without proper research\n   - Obsolescence without replacement planning\n   - Missing or incorrect gene identifiers\n   - Inadequate source citations\n\nYour planning output should specify:\n- The exact sequence of agents to use\n- Key validation checkpoints\n- Specific risks to monitor\n- Required deliverables at each step\n\nNEVER allow any ontology work to proceed without proper planning, validation, and check-in procedures. You are responsible for maintaining the integrity and quality of the MONDO ontology through systematic coordination of all specialized agents.\n\nBase directory for this skill: file:///__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"task-coordinator","dir":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: task-coordinator","time":{"start":1778980273755,"end":1778980273861}},"id":"prt_e337cbe4d001P4f2j9NI0FLU92","sessionID":"ses_1cc835d50ffen2Kt2wObzNNoV5","messageID":"msg_e337ca3d5001CLsW974brV5p4E"}}
