{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778980554555,"sessionID":"ses_1cc835d50ffen2Kt2wObzNNoV5","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_CxmKxCA21Es9Ygxv5HF0YRRy","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n+Addressed in PR #<NN>.\n+\n+Added the requested umbrella terms `cardiogenetic rhythm disorder` and `SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder`, and placed the requested child terms under them. I followed the clarification in the issue comments by excluding `atrioventricular block` from the broad cardiogenetic grouping and by using the revised definitions without multifocal ectopic Purkinje-related premature contractions.\n+\n+Note: I was able to run a local `robot convert` syntax check successfully, but I could not run the required ODK `make NORM` normalization in this environment because Docker is unavailable.\n*** Add File: PR_COMMENTS.md\n+Implemented the issue 9707 request in `src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo`.\n+\n+Changes made:\n+\n+- Added new term `MONDO:7770003` `cardiogenetic rhythm disorder` under `MONDO:0100547` `cardiogenetic disease`.\n+- Added new term `MONDO:7770004` `SCN5A-related cardiac rhythm disorder` under:\n+  - `MONDO:0007263` `cardiac rhythm disease`\n+  - `MONDO:0100547` `cardiogenetic disease`\n+  - `MONDO:7770003` `cardiogenetic rhythm disorder`\n+- Added `has_material_basis_in_germline_mutation_in` for `SCN5A` on `MONDO:7770004` using the OMIM-backed SCN5A child terms cited in the issue.\n+- Added subclass assertions to place the requested SCN5A-specific terms under `MONDO:7770004`:\n+  - `MONDO:0013530` atrial fibrillation, familial, 10\n+  - `MONDO:0024562` sick sinus syndrome 1\n+  - `MONDO:0011376` ventricular fibrillation, paroxysmal familial, type 1\n+  - `MONDO:0011377` long QT syndrome 3\n+  - `MONDO:0011001` Brugada syndrome 1\n+- Added subclass assertions to place the requested broad monogenic rhythm terms under `MONDO:7770003`:\n+  - `MONDO:0014500` atrial conduction disease\n+  - `MONDO:0015263` Brugada syndrome\n+  - `MONDO:0018054` familial atrial fibrillation\n+  - `MONDO:0012061` familial sick sinus syndrome\n+  - `MONDO:0019490` progressive familial heart block\n+  - `MONDO:0000453` short QT syndrome\n+  - `MONDO:0008648` ventricular tachycardia, familial\n+  - `MONDO:0011376` ventricular fibrillation, paroxysmal familial, type 1\n+\n+Issue-thread decisions followed:\n+\n+- Used the revised definitions from the comment by `@LengUNC`, so the new definitions do not include multifocal ectopic Purkinje-related premature contractions.\n+- Did not add `atrioventricular block (MONDO:0000465)` as a child of `cardiogenetic rhythm disorder`, matching the prior discussion that it is not necessarily monogenic.\n+\n+Validation and workflow notes:\n+\n+- Reviewed the imported issue context and existing ontology state before editing.\n+- Used `obo-checkout.pl` / `obo-checkin.pl` workflow rather than direct manual editing of the large OBO file.\n+- Ran local syntax validation with:\n+  - `robot convert --catalog src/ontology/catalog-v001.xml -i src/ontology/mondo-edit.obo -f obo -o mondo-edit.TMP.obo`\n+- Could not run required ODK normalization `make NORM` in this environment because Docker is not available (`docker: command not found`).\n+\n+Completed checklist:\n+\n+- [x] Read issue title, body, and comments from `__issue_context__.json`\n+- [x] Verified current ontology state for requested terms\n+- [x] Added the two requested new terms with revised definitions\n+- [x] Hooked up requested child terms to the new groupings\n+- [x] Preserved the issue-thread exclusion of `atrioventricular block`\n+- [x] Ran a local syntax conversion check\n+- [x] Committed only the ontology file change\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\nA PR_COMMENTS.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\n======================================================